used only to describe compatibility.

Third-party references
----------------------

* The Linux aquacomputer_d5next hwmon driver, GPL-2.0-or-later, by Aleksa Savic, Jack Doan,
  Leonard Anderweit and contributors (drivers/hwmon/aquacomputer_d5next.c in the kernel, and the
  extended version at https://github.com/aleksamagicka/aquacomputer_d5next-hwmon with its
  reverse-engineering notes in re-docs/). Used as the reference for the report layouts, offsets,
  checksums, the "save" report, fan control modes, curve and power-limit fields, and the Aquaero,
  Aquastream XT and Leakshield specifics. No code is copied; the protocol facts were reimplemented
  in Python.

* The captured QUADRO reports in tests/data/ (quadro_control.bin, quadro_sensors.bin,
  quadro_virt_sensors.bin) come from that repository's re-docs/quadro directory
  (contributed by Leonard Anderweit) and are used as test fixtures.

* liquidctl (https://github.com/liquidctl/liquidctl), GPL-3.0-or-later, by Jonas Malaco and
  contributors, whose Aquacomputer driver by Aleksa Savic documents the direct manual-mode write.
  Used as a reference only.

* The user interface shares its design system (colour tokens, style sheet, icon style and small
  widgets) with the author's ReolinkLinux, EZP2019Linux and FirmwareLab applications (MIT).

